411
00:29:29.069 --> 00:29:29.986
Part 4.

412
00:29:30.266 --> 00:29:34.085
Design Document Excerpt: gro.cr Short-Link Service.

413
00:29:35.335 --> 00:29:36.081
Note:

414
00:29:36.361 --> 00:29:39.647
Design Document (excerpt), Short-Link Service v2.

415
00:29:39.927 --> 00:29:40.823
Status:

416
00:29:41.103 --> 00:29:42.383
Accepted, Authors:

417
00:29:42.663 --> 00:29:44.689
Messaging platform team, Reviewers:

418
00:29:44.969 --> 00:29:47.316
Security, SRE, Marketing tech.

419
00:29:47.596 --> 00:30:01.975
Context, v1 used sequential codes (enumerable), 301 redirects (lost analytics), one shared pool (campaign spike broke order tracking), synchronous counters, and unrestricted destinations (phishing).

420
00:30:02.255 --> 00:30:06.095
TRAI DLT requires whitelisted URLs in SMS.

421
00:30:06.375 --> 00:30:28.156
Decision, 7-char codes from block-allocated counters through a keyed Feistel permutation; 302 redirects; allow-listed https destinations; idempotent create; near-cache + Redis + partitioned PostgreSQL; clicks via Kafka to a stream aggregator with HLL uniques; separate redirect deployment.

422
00:30:29.506 --> 00:30:54.594
Related ADRs, ADR-240 Code scheme: counter blocks + permutation (L1); ADR-241 302 + no-store for redirects; ADR-242 Destination allow-list and idempotent create (L2); ADR-243 Three-tier read path with 1 s near-cache and campaign pre-warm (L3); ADR-244 Async click pipeline,

423
00:30:54.874 --> 00:31:13.946
HLL for uniques (L4); ADR-245 PostgreSQL partitioned by expiry month; KV store when live set exceeds ~2 TB or multi-region writes needed; ADR-246 No code recycling; 410 after expiry.

424
00:31:14.226 --> 00:31:15.186
Requirements.

425
00:31:15.466 --> 00:31:23.210
R1 Redirect p99 20 ms server-side, 99.95% availability per region.

426
00:31:24.560 --> 00:31:31.216
R2 Survive a 100M-SMS campaign on a single code without affecting transactional links.

427
00:31:31.496 --> 00:31:38.877
R3 No destination outside the allow-list; no enumerable codes; nothing personal in codes or URLs.

428
00:31:39.157 --> 00:31:43.787
R4 Create is idempotent; bulk create 20M links in under an hour.

429
00:31:44.067 --> 00:31:48.376
R5 Click counts within 1 minute; unique visitors within 2%.

430
00:31:48.656 --> 00:31:50.064
Decisions in detail.

431
00:31:51.414 --> 00:31:53.526
Codes (ADR-240).

432
00:31:53.806 --> 00:32:04.729
Blocks of 1,000 from a sequence; 4-round Feistel over 62^7 with keys in the secrets manager; custom aliases from a separate namespace with a reserved list.

433
00:32:05.009 --> 00:32:07.547
Redirects (ADR-241).

434
00:32:07.827 --> 00:32:18.345
302 with Cache-Control: private, max-age=0; 410 for expired or revoked; 404 negative-cached for 60 s.

435
00:32:18.625 --> 00:32:21.099
Write path (ADR-242).

436
00:32:21.379 --> 00:32:30.019
URL parsed with the platform's URL library; https, no user-info, exact host match; unique (owner, urlhash).

437
00:32:30.299 --> 00:32:32.859
Read path (ADR-243).

438
00:32:33.139 --> 00:32:44.019
Caffeine near-cache 1 s TTL (10k entries); Redis TTL 24 h; miss coalescing per code; campaign codes pre-warmed 10 min before send.

439
00:32:45.369 --> 00:32:47.951
Analytics (ADR-244).

440
00:32:48.231 --> 00:32:58.108
Click events to Kafka link-clicks keyed by code; Flink per-minute aggregates + HLL (p = 14) per link per day; bots flagged by UA list.

441
00:32:58.388 --> 00:33:00.863
Storage (ADR-245).

442
00:33:01.143 --> 00:33:06.988
Monthly partitions by expiresat; permanent links in a never partition; two read replicas.

443
00:33:07.268 --> 00:33:08.292
Consequences.

444
00:33:08.572 --> 00:33:13.969
302 means every click is served, so the read path's cost is the design's centre.

445
00:33:14.249 --> 00:33:15.721
Counts lag by seconds.

446
00:33:16.001 --> 00:33:18.327
Codes are 7 characters, not 5.

447
00:33:18.607 --> 00:33:24.537
In exchange: private links, working analytics, isolation from campaigns, and bounded storage.

448
00:33:25.887 --> 00:33:26.847
