00:34:33.472 --> 00:34:35.691
L1, Four ways to mint a short code.

459
00:34:35.971 --> 00:34:36.909
Requirement:

460
00:34:37.189 --> 00:34:39.600
Every order-tracking SMS carries a link.

461
00:34:39.880 --> 00:34:45.597
Codes must be short, unique, cheap to mint, and must not let one customer find another's order.

462
00:34:45.877 --> 00:34:47.968
Two million codes are minted four ways.

463
00:34:48.248 --> 00:35:00.941
The permutation is a 4-round Feistel network on 42 bits with cycle-walking to stay within 62^7, a bijection, so uniqueness is guaranteed without storing or checking anything.

464
